# Pairs with EventualConvergence. A saga commits at the origin without logging its terminal, so the
# receiver, which holds a prepared write invisible until its terminal lands, never applies it, and the
# watermark stays clamped below the prepare.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceCommitLogsNoTerminal
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a committed saga ships no terminal, so its write never becomes visible at the receiver
PERTURBS: CommitA
BOUNDS: NParts = 1, Sagas = TRUE

--- FIND
    /\ alog' = [alog EXCEPT ![p] = Append(@, [k |-> "term", h |-> h])]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: no terminal is logged.
    /\ UNCHANGED alog
--- END
